 "text": "..title\nA resolution to appropriate grant funds from the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services to the Metropolitan Government, acting by and through the Metropolitan Action Commission, to support Head Start and Early Head Start developmental activities for disadvantaged children, food service for nutritional needs, and equipment purchases for the seven sites.     \n..body\nWHEREAS, the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services has awarded a grant in an amount not to exceed $17,999,350 with a required cash match of $4,499,837 to the Metropolitan Government, acting by and through the Metropolitan Action Commission, to support Head Start and Early Head Start developmental activities for disadvantaged children, food service for nutritional needs, and equipment purchases for the seven sites,  \nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Action Commission has accepted this grant pursuant to its authority under Metro Code of Laws section 2.108.050; and,\nWHEREAS, it is to the benefit of the citizens of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County that these funds be appropriated to the Metropolitan Action Commission.\nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThat the funds from a grant by and between the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services, in an amount not to exceed $17,999,350, to the Metropolitan Government, acting by and through the Metropolitan Action Commission, t to support Head Start and Early Head Start developmental activities for disadvantaged children, food service for nutritional needs, and equipment purchases for the seven sites, a copy of which grant is attached hereto and incorporated herein, be appropriated to the Metropolitan Action Commission.\nSection 2.\tThat this resolution shall take effect from and after its adoption, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis resolution accepts a grant from the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services to the Metropolitan Action Commission. The grant will fund Head Start and Early Head Start developmental activities, food service, and equipment purchases. The Head Start and Early Head Start programs serve 1,163 disadvantaged children between ages 0 and 5.\n\nThe grant award is for an amount not to exceed $17,999,350, with a required cash match of $4,499,837. The grant term is effective on July 1, 2026, and would end on June 30, 2027.\n\n"
}
